{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments ["<b>And they shall know that I am YHWH their Elohim who brought them out of the land of Egypt to dwell in their midst.</b> He says that the bringing out was on condition of dwelling in their midst, for had it not been so He would not have brought them out. And this shows that the indwelling of the Shekhinah among Israel is a need of the Most High — not a need of the lowly. And this is, in my opinion, what the prophet Hosea, peace be upon him, said (Hosea 13:4): ״ואנכי ה׳ אלהיך מארץ מצרים ואלהים זולתי לא תדע ומושיע אין בלתי״ — that is, I did not bring you out of the land of Egypt except for the sake of 'I am YHWH your Elohim,' so that you would accept My divinity upon yourself, and so that you would not know any Elohim besides Me; and therefore He mentioned 'from the land of Egypt' in the middle." "<b>And so</b> I found in the Midrash Tehillim on the verse (Psalms 114:1): ״בצאת ישראל ממצרים״ — Rabbi Yehoshua ben Levi said: by the merit of the Mishkan Israel were redeemed from Egypt, as it is said (Exodus 2:25): ״וירא אלהים את בני ישראל״, and it is written (Exodus 39:43): ״וירא משה את כל המלאכה״." "<b>There is</b> also another place from which to learn that 'I brought you out of the land of Egypt on the condition to dwell in their midst' — thus far the language of the Midrash. And this is what is written (Psalms 132:14): ״אוה למושב לו״, and it is written (ibid.): ״פה אשב כי אויתיה״. And the verses that testify to this are numerous, and I have already mentioned this at the verse 'and He spoke' (וידבר)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:33.105148033Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}